  "rationale": [
    "Reused LineupLayout.scaleFor(Size) without multiplying by DPR.",
    "Scaled _osdAction itself and wrapped individual option actions for enlarged system text so the real button geometry remains proportional and bounded.",
    "Scaled only Player OSD geometry, typography, artwork caller bounds, progress lane, channel bug, and native button hit regions.",
    "Kept gradient colors, stops, opacity, callbacks, focus nodes, overlay transitions, artwork loading and fallback policy unchanged.",
    "Preserved the normal-text Row action layout; enlarged system text uses a width-constrained Wrap of the existing action groups."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Captures are synthetic portable macOS Flutter widget evidence with portable test fonts, not physical Windows evidence.",
    "Moving video, DirectComposition/native layering, native Windows input/focus, monitor-DPI transitions, HDR and packaging remain unvalidated.",
    "No tracked tests or documentation were added; the capture harness and this report are ignored evidence artifacts.",
    "The full PlayerView suite's track-panel assertion remains stale relative to the already-integrated uncapped shared scaling helper and was not changed under the OSD-only lease."
